2. Petitioner approached this Court in WP(C) No.33161/2014 seeking the following reliefs:-
" i) to issue a writ of certiorari or any other appropriate writ or order quashing Exhibit P2 notification and Exhibit P3 declaration in so far as it relate to the land of the petitioner and Exts. P5,
P5(a), P5(b), P5(c), P5(d), P5(e), P5(f) & P5(g) awards;
 ii) to issue a writ of mandamus or  any other appropriate writ or order  declaring that the acquisition proceedings taken against the land of the petitioner under Exhibit P2 notification is vitiated by limitation under the 1st proviso to Section 6(1) and lapsed under Section 11A of the Land Acquisition Act, 1894 conferring no right or title to respondents 1 & 4 over the land;
 iii) to issue a writ of mandamus or  WP(C) NO. 38102 OF 2016  2025:KER:39914  any other appropriate writ or order directing the respondents to restore the possession and ownership of the petitioner over the land comprised in Sy.No.174 of Pallipuram village, Cherthala Taluk and covered under Exhibit P2 P.M.Fathima Barkath vs The State Of Kerala on 4 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/33843624/
2 notification;
iv) to issue a writ of mandamus or any other appropriate writ or order directing the respondents 1 and 2 to take a decision of Exhibits P10, P13 representations filed by the petitioner;
 and  v) to issue such other appropriate writ, order or directions as this Hon'ble Court may deem just and proper to issue in the circumstances of the case."
